---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { ArrowLeft } from "lucide-astro";

const lastUpdated = "September 18, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy - Marcel Lassance"
  description="What this site collects, and what it does not."
>
  <main class="max-w-[720px] mx-auto px-8 py-20">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-accent no-underline text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.1em] transition-colors duration-300 hover:text-text"
    >
      <ArrowLeft size={16} class="shrink-0" />
      <span>Back</span>
    </a>

    <h1 class="text-4xl mt-12 mb-2">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-accent text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.1em]">
      Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <p class="mt-12 leading-[1.8]">
      This is a portfolio site. There are no accounts, no forms, and nothing to
      sign in to. It sets no cookies and collects no analytics. What follows is
      the short list of everything else that happens when you open a page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base mt-12 mb-3">Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8]">
      None of either. Nothing is written to cookies or browser storage, no
      analytics or tracking service runs here, and there is no consent banner
      because there is nothing to consent to. Script errors are not reported
      anywhere either.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base mt-12 mb-3">Fonts and hosting</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8]">
      The typefaces are served by Google Fonts, and the site itself is served by
      GitHub Pages. Loading a page therefore makes a request to each of them,
      and both see the standard technical details any web server sees, your IP
      address among them, as part of answering it. Neither is asked to do
      anything beyond delivering the page and its fonts.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base mt-12 mb-3">Getting in touch</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8]">
      The contact details on this site are an email address and an Instagram
      handle, not a form. Writing to either is the ordinary thing it appears to
      be, and nothing you send is stored anywhere other than the inbox it
      arrives in.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-base mt-12 mb-3">Changes</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8]">
      If this policy changes, the new version is posted on this page with a new
      date at the top.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
